        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Vefa, Golden Horn\n- Structures: Kalenderhane Mosque, Galata Bridge, Aqueduct of Valens, Vefa Kilise, Süleymaniye Mosque\n- Concepts: Eastern Orthodox church, mosque, Byzantine monuments, Ottoman monuments\n\nFacts:\n- Kalenderhane Mosque in Istanbul is a former Eastern Orthodox church.\n- Kalenderhane Mosque in Istanbul was converted into a mosque by the Ottomans.\n- Galata Bridge spans the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Vefa lies roughly northwest of the eastern section of the Aqueduct of Valens.\n- Vefa is rich in Byzantine monuments such as Kalenderhane Mosque and Vefa Kilise.\n- Vefa is rich in Ottoman monuments such as Süleymaniye Mosque.",
